1
00:00:02,480 --> 00:00:05,350
April Only

2
00:00:08,440 --> 00:00:10,610
Oh, yummy!

3
00:00:10,990 --> 00:00:14,360
<i>Springtime means cherry blossom sweets!</i>

4
00:00:17,370 --> 00:00:21,250
What do you want to do 
for your birthday next week, Hananoi-kun?

5
00:00:21,250 --> 00:00:24,790
It's the perfect time to go see the cherry
blossoms. How does that sound?

6
00:00:24,790 --> 00:00:29,290
That sounds great! Are there any 
good viewing spots around here?

7
00:00:30,130 --> 00:00:32,700
Oh, this place might be nice.

8
00:00:32,700 --> 00:00:36,300
It's kinda far, but it should 
be walkable from here.

9
00:00:34,880 --> 00:00:38,890
Recommended!

10
00:00:34,880 --> 00:00:38,890
A hidden spot that even few locals know about.
It is somewhat far from the station, but that means
there aren't many tourists and you can relax and
enjoy flower viewing. Definitely worth a visit to see
the cherry blossoms floating in the river.

11
00:00:34,880 --> 00:00:38,890
From exit 2 of the station, it's basically
a straight shot. It takes about 13 minutes
walking, but that'll give you a chance
to enjoy the scenery along the way.

12
00:00:36,300 --> 00:00:38,900
Wow, that's so pretty!

13
00:00:39,230 --> 00:00:40,600
Let's go there!

14
00:00:45,270 --> 00:00:49,270
I guess I could... try making 
a picnic lunch or something.

15
00:00:49,270 --> 00:00:50,860
R-Really?

16
00:00:51,360 --> 00:00:53,150
D-Don't expect too much, though.

17
00:00:53,440 --> 00:00:54,990
I'm so happy!

18
00:00:55,450 --> 00:00:57,110
I can't wait!

19
00:02:28,660 --> 00:02:34,960
Episode 9

20
00:02:28,660 --> 00:02:34,960
His First Birthday

21
00:02:35,960 --> 00:02:38,260
Hello? Grandma?

22
00:02:38,920 --> 00:02:39,680
Yeah.

23
00:02:41,220 --> 00:02:43,140
Yeah, I'm okay.

24
00:02:43,680 --> 00:02:46,600
I still have some meals left, so don't worry.

25
00:02:46,600 --> 00:02:50,940
<i>Listen... I received a letter from Chizuru.</i>

26
00:02:50,940 --> 00:02:53,270
Oh, I got one too.

27
00:02:53,650 --> 00:02:57,990
Mom and Dad say they aren't 
coming home this spring.

28
00:02:57,990 --> 00:03:02,530
<i>Gracious. Do they even care
about their son's birthday?</i>

29
00:03:03,120 --> 00:03:05,990
<i>So, what are you doing on the 6th?</i>

30
00:03:05,990 --> 00:03:09,660
<i>If you don't have any plans, want to 
come over? I'll cook you up a feast.</i>

31
00:03:10,080 --> 00:03:11,170
That's okay.

32
00:03:11,620 --> 00:03:13,920
I'm planning to spend the day
 with my girlfriend.

33
00:03:13,920 --> 00:03:18,050
<i>Oh, is that right? 
Well, I suppose that's fine, then.</i>

34
00:03:18,050 --> 00:03:21,550
<i>I know it's your birthday, 
but don't get too carried away, okay?</i>

35
00:03:21,550 --> 00:03:24,220
<i>You'd better be sure to send 
her home at an early hour!</i>

36
00:03:24,220 --> 00:03:27,060
<i>And it still gets cold at night, 
so wear something warm—</i>

37
00:03:31,060 --> 00:03:34,560
Hinase Hotaru

38
00:03:31,060 --> 00:03:34,560
The weekly forecast says
the 6th should be sunny!
I'm so glad!

39
00:03:35,150 --> 00:03:39,820
<i>I've never been so excited about a 
birthday before. This is a first for me.</i>

40
00:03:44,320 --> 00:03:47,830
Hananoi

41
00:03:44,320 --> 00:03:47,830
Thanks for today

42
00:03:44,320 --> 00:03:47,830
The scones were delicious!

43
00:03:44,320 --> 00:03:47,830
The weekly forecast says
the 6th should be sunny!
I'm so glad!

44
00:03:44,320 --> 00:03:47,830
The sakura trees should be
in full bloom too. I can't wait.

45
00:03:48,160 --> 00:03:49,450
Hmm.

46
00:03:50,120 --> 00:03:52,500
<i>A present, a picnic lunch...</i>

47
00:03:53,460 --> 00:03:56,170
<i>I wonder if there's anything else I can do.</i>

48
00:03:56,880 --> 00:04:01,840
<i>It's the perfect opportunity. I want to do 
something to make him super happy.</i>

49
00:04:02,970 --> 00:04:04,260
One day,

50
00:04:05,010 --> 00:04:08,010
when we finally share a real kiss,

51
00:04:09,100 --> 00:04:11,850
I want you to be as elated as I will be.

52
00:04:12,810 --> 00:04:18,400
So when your heart is ready for it
and you decide you want it,

53
00:04:19,270 --> 00:04:20,730
give me a signal, okay?

54
00:04:22,030 --> 00:04:23,360
<i>A signal...</i>

55
00:04:24,030 --> 00:04:28,660
<i>No, wait! He was saying I should think 
about it without feeling pressured, right?</i>

56
00:04:31,000 --> 00:04:35,750
<i>But still, if he asks me if 
I want to kiss him again...</i>

57
00:04:36,670 --> 00:04:38,630
<i>I'm not sure I get it.</i>

58
00:04:39,710 --> 00:04:44,630
<i>When he kissed my forehead, 
I felt more embarrassed than anything.</i>

59
00:04:45,760 --> 00:04:49,470
<i>What makes people want 
to kiss in the first place?</i>

60
00:04:50,720 --> 00:04:52,480
So, considering the situation,

61
00:04:52,810 --> 00:04:55,730
what wisdom might you be able 
to share with me, Big Sis?

62
00:04:56,230 --> 00:05:00,570
<i>Why does this kid keep coming 
to me for advice like that?</i>

63
00:05:01,400 --> 00:05:03,240
I'm sorry to bother you.

64
00:05:03,650 --> 00:05:07,030
But I'm way too embarrassed 
to ask my friends.

65
00:05:10,990 --> 00:05:15,370
Oh, kissing? Yeah, that's easy. Listen up.

66
00:05:15,710 --> 00:05:19,500
When you like someone, you want 
to be close to them, right?

67
00:05:19,500 --> 00:05:20,920
It's the next step from that.

68
00:05:22,050 --> 00:05:23,460
I see.

69
00:05:24,550 --> 00:05:25,420
<i>I think.</i>

70
00:05:25,840 --> 00:05:27,220
<i>Not that I'd know.</i>

71
00:05:29,350 --> 00:05:32,560
So a kiss is the next step up 
from wanting to touch him?

72
00:05:32,970 --> 00:05:34,530
Oh, Hotaru.

73
00:05:34,890 --> 00:05:39,020
Remember the memorial service we've been 
planning for Grandpa? It'll be on the 6th.

74
00:05:39,360 --> 00:05:42,400
Yeah? I guess it is that time of year.

75
00:05:43,280 --> 00:05:46,900
Oh, wait. Do you mean April 6th?

76
00:05:46,900 --> 00:05:47,860
Yup.

77
00:05:49,990 --> 00:05:54,950
<i>Sorry! Wh-What should we do?
 I thought I was free!</i>

78
00:05:54,950 --> 00:05:58,500
Hmm, well, you've got the memorial service.

79
00:05:58,500 --> 00:06:01,420
You probably won't be in the 
mood to celebrate anyway.

80
00:06:01,920 --> 00:06:03,420
Let's do it another day.

81
00:06:03,420 --> 00:06:08,290
But I don't have any other days off when the
 cherry blossoms will still be in bloom.

82
00:06:08,630 --> 00:06:10,590
And school's starting soon.

83
00:06:10,590 --> 00:06:12,050
<i>It's okay.</i>

84
00:06:12,050 --> 00:06:14,890
<i>As long as we can celebrate 
together, Hotaru-chan,</i>

85
00:06:14,890 --> 00:06:18,290
<i>the time and place don't matter. 
I'm still going to be happy.</i>

86
00:06:22,110 --> 00:06:27,190
Well, Hotaru, you didn't know Grandpa 
that well. You don't have to go.

87
00:06:30,320 --> 00:06:32,910
No. I'll go.

88
00:06:32,910 --> 00:06:34,200
Are you sure?

89
00:06:36,160 --> 00:06:39,710
It is what it is...

90
00:06:49,720 --> 00:06:51,840
Dismiss

91
00:06:49,720 --> 00:06:51,970
Snooze

92
00:06:49,720 --> 00:06:52,340
April 6

93
00:06:49,720 --> 00:06:52,340
Alarm

94
00:06:56,470 --> 00:07:02,980
Hananoi-kun,
happy birthday!

95
00:07:01,480 --> 00:07:02,980
Thanks

96
00:07:05,070 --> 00:07:06,190
<i>Okay.</i>

97
00:07:06,900 --> 00:07:08,570
<i>What'll I do today?</i>

98
00:07:15,450 --> 00:07:17,870
<i>I've pretty much finished up here.</i>

99
00:07:19,870 --> 00:07:22,880
<i>I guess I'll go check it out by myself.</i>

100
00:07:27,550 --> 00:07:30,090
<i>Maybe I can bring her here next year.</i>

101
00:07:31,510 --> 00:07:33,390
Wow, that looks good!

102
00:07:31,510 --> 00:07:35,260
Takoyaki

103
00:07:31,800 --> 00:07:33,590
<i>I didn't know they had food stands.</i>

104
00:07:33,390 --> 00:07:35,260
Well, this one is on me.

105
00:07:35,260 --> 00:07:38,220
Thank you! I was craving some takoyaki.

106
00:07:38,220 --> 00:07:39,520
Really? It's your lucky day.

107
00:07:50,490 --> 00:07:54,200
<i>There aren't many people 
over here by the river.</i>

108
00:08:09,710 --> 00:08:12,880
Ah, it's finally over!

109
00:08:12,880 --> 00:08:14,010
Watch it, Tomo!

110
00:08:14,510 --> 00:08:17,680
<i>It took two hours to get here by train.</i>

111
00:08:18,310 --> 00:08:22,770
<i>If we leave before it gets dark, I might 
still have a little time to see him.</i>

112
00:08:23,800 --> 00:08:25,980
U-Um, Mom?

113
00:08:25,980 --> 00:08:26,730
Hmm?

114
00:08:26,730 --> 00:08:28,230
What's next?

115
00:08:28,230 --> 00:08:31,780
Next, the plan is to go to 
a hotel for dinner with everyone.

116
00:08:34,570 --> 00:08:37,740
<i>It's guaranteed to be night 
before we get back!</i>

117
00:08:39,120 --> 00:08:42,160
What's got you so anxious, Hotaru?

118
00:08:42,160 --> 00:08:47,290
Well, to tell you the truth...
today is my boyfriend's birthday.

119
00:08:48,960 --> 00:08:50,670
Then why not leave already?

120
00:08:50,670 --> 00:08:51,430
Huh?

121
00:08:51,840 --> 00:08:55,840
You're in high school.
 You can find your way back, right?

122
00:08:55,840 --> 00:08:56,920
B-But...

123
00:08:57,550 --> 00:09:00,850
It'll just be adults blabbing after this.

124
00:09:00,850 --> 00:09:03,140
There's no reason the kids have to be there.

125
00:09:03,640 --> 00:09:06,230
I'll make up some excuse to tell Dad.

126
00:09:08,230 --> 00:09:09,980
Is that really okay?

127
00:09:12,480 --> 00:09:15,990
You know, you've seemed a lot
happier lately, Hotaru.

128
00:09:16,450 --> 00:09:21,830
Tomo and I are so loud,
 it always felt like you were holding back.

129
00:09:22,330 --> 00:09:27,210
But you should be able to do 
what you want, too.

130
00:09:27,960 --> 00:09:32,380
Grandpa wouldn't want to see you sad, 
either. Don't you think you should go?

131
00:09:35,800 --> 00:09:42,010
I mean, it's his birthday. 
You only get your day once a year.

132
00:09:43,310 --> 00:09:47,520
I feel like those twenty-four hours
should be totally dedicated to you.

133
00:09:48,440 --> 00:09:50,900
It should be a super special time for him.

134
00:09:52,270 --> 00:09:55,490
And... I'm only just now realizing that.

135
00:09:55,900 --> 00:09:58,030
Yeah, I bet.

136
00:09:58,030 --> 00:10:01,450
If you make it a special day,
I'm sure he'll love that.

137
00:10:09,500 --> 00:10:15,010
Sis! I... I really have to go today!

138
00:10:15,420 --> 00:10:16,550
Roger that.

139
00:10:17,220 --> 00:10:18,800
Leave things here to me.

140
00:10:20,640 --> 00:10:23,970
Sis, you really are the best!

141
00:10:29,190 --> 00:10:32,150
Happy birthday, Hotaru-chan.

142
00:10:33,150 --> 00:10:37,740
I hope today turned out
 to be special for you.

143
00:10:41,570 --> 00:10:46,580
But it had to be today. I wanted you to know

144
00:10:47,450 --> 00:10:52,670
that today is the most 
special day in the world.

145
00:10:58,760 --> 00:10:59,930
<i>Me too!</i>

146
00:11:11,940 --> 00:11:13,270
<i>Hananoi-kun!</i>

147
00:11:23,910 --> 00:11:24,480
Hello.

148
00:11:24,480 --> 00:11:27,450
<i>Hey, Hananoi? It's me, Kurata!</i>

149
00:11:33,540 --> 00:11:36,130
How the hell did you get my number?

150
00:11:36,130 --> 00:11:38,540
<i>Oh, come on! You forgot already?</i>

151
00:11:38,880 --> 00:11:42,680
I asked you to call me
 when I lost my phone in class!

152
00:11:42,680 --> 00:11:43,890
<i>You forced me to.</i>

153
00:11:43,890 --> 00:11:45,640
You saved my butt, man!

154
00:11:45,640 --> 00:11:47,640
<i>And then you secretly saved my number?</i>

155
00:11:47,640 --> 00:11:48,900
No big deal.

156
00:11:48,900 --> 00:11:52,270
Actually, I wanted to ask you something 
about our spring break homework.

157
00:11:52,270 --> 00:11:56,150
Oh, also, I heard from Hibiki.
Isn't today your birthday?

158
00:11:56,150 --> 00:11:57,110
Happy birthday, man!

159
00:11:57,440 --> 00:11:58,780
<i>And let me guess.</i>

160
00:11:58,780 --> 00:12:00,990
<i>Are you hanging with Hinase-san?</i>

161
00:12:02,490 --> 00:12:03,490
No, I'm not.

162
00:12:03,490 --> 00:12:05,950
<i>Wait, what? No way! That's so sad!</i>

163
00:12:05,950 --> 00:12:09,160
Dude, would you lay off it?

164
00:12:09,160 --> 00:12:13,960
<i>What? But this is your first birthday
with her. That's gotta hurt.</i>

165
00:12:13,960 --> 00:12:16,250
Hotaru-chan had something else going on.

166
00:12:16,840 --> 00:12:19,840
If we can celebrate some other 
time, that's good enough.

167
00:12:19,840 --> 00:12:22,630
<i>Wow, maybe you are a good guy.</i>

168
00:12:23,500 --> 00:12:25,930
<i>You always come off so possessive,</i>

169
00:12:25,930 --> 00:12:28,720
<i>but I guess you know when to back off.
 I underestimated you!</i>

170
00:12:29,180 --> 00:12:30,270
I'm hanging up.

171
00:12:30,270 --> 00:12:32,020
<i>Hey, wait! The homework!</i>

172
00:12:35,600 --> 00:12:37,690
<i>What part of me is a "good guy"?</i>

173
00:12:45,860 --> 00:12:47,780
Oh, a butterfly!

174
00:12:48,160 --> 00:12:50,700
You're right! It sure is pretty.

175
00:12:50,700 --> 00:12:51,660
Yeah!

176
00:14:01,150 --> 00:14:03,650
How have you

177
00:14:01,150 --> 00:14:03,650
Are you doing

178
00:14:01,150 --> 00:14:03,650
Is Grandma

179
00:14:25,420 --> 00:14:26,880
It's time to go!

180
00:14:26,880 --> 00:14:27,880
Okay!

181
00:14:37,350 --> 00:14:38,770
<i>I've been trying to find</i>

182
00:14:39,440 --> 00:14:43,730
<i>someone who needs me. 
More than family, more than a friend.</i>

183
00:14:44,730 --> 00:14:48,110
<i>I was looking for someone who 
would always put me first.</i>

184
00:14:49,740 --> 00:14:51,950
<i>I would've done anything 
for someone like that.</i>

185
00:14:53,620 --> 00:15:00,290
<i>But even when I give all my love to people,
they never put me first.</i>

186
00:15:02,420 --> 00:15:06,050
<i>And if I can't be their number one, 
then what's the point?</i>

187
00:15:07,840 --> 00:15:12,550
<i>That's all I ever think about. 
How does that make me a "good guy"?</i>

188
00:15:19,390 --> 00:15:21,810
<i>Still, I don't know why,</i>

189
00:15:28,360 --> 00:15:30,360
<i>but when I'm with Hotaru-chan,</i>

190
00:15:31,490 --> 00:15:35,240
<i>there are moments when I stop 
caring about being number one.</i>

191
00:15:35,870 --> 00:15:40,580
<i>Her smile is enough for me. 
That alone makes me feel complete.</i>

192
00:15:49,380 --> 00:15:51,130
<i>I want you to keep smiling.</i>

193
00:15:52,720 --> 00:15:55,510
<i>Don't look at anyone else.</i>

194
00:15:56,140 --> 00:15:57,720
<i>I don't want you to hate me.</i>

195
00:15:59,350 --> 00:16:01,140
<i>Don't leave me.</i>

196
00:16:04,810 --> 00:16:08,280
<i>My feelings... I'm a mess.</i>

197
00:16:14,660 --> 00:16:17,160
Hotaru-chan

198
00:16:14,660 --> 00:16:17,160
Hananoi-kun, where are you?

199
00:16:19,830 --> 00:16:21,750
H-He isn't here.

200
00:16:26,130 --> 00:16:30,420
<i>I couldn't get him on the phone 
either. Where could he be?</i>

201
00:16:31,010 --> 00:16:34,010
<i>Weird. It's usually the other way around.</i>

202
00:16:35,050 --> 00:16:39,720
<i>It's always Hananoi-kun 
who comes running to look for me.</i>

203
00:16:43,850 --> 00:16:45,560
I don't want you to leave me behind.

204
00:16:50,030 --> 00:16:51,780
Hananoi

205
00:16:50,030 --> 00:16:51,780
Hananoi-kun,
where are you?

206
00:16:50,030 --> 00:16:51,780
I'm at home

207
00:16:51,780 --> 00:16:52,950
Huh?!

208
00:17:03,300 --> 00:17:07,280
<i>Why would he lie about where he is?</i>

209
00:17:29,520 --> 00:17:30,810
<i>I won't leave you behind.</i>

210
00:17:31,480 --> 00:17:33,070
<i>I won't leave you behind!</i>

211
00:17:34,490 --> 00:17:34,900
Hananoi-kun,
where are you?

212
00:17:34,490 --> 00:17:34,900
I'm at home

213
00:17:34,900 --> 00:17:36,490
I'm at home

214
00:17:34,900 --> 00:17:36,490
I'm on my way now

215
00:17:36,780 --> 00:17:40,490
Oh! Huh? Should I go home?

216
00:17:40,490 --> 00:17:44,000
I'm at home

217
00:17:40,490 --> 00:17:44,000
Hinase Hotaru

218
00:17:40,490 --> 00:17:44,000
I'm on my way now

219
00:17:40,490 --> 00:17:44,000
Stay right where you are!

220
00:17:44,000 --> 00:17:46,750
Hinase Hotaru

221
00:17:44,000 --> 00:17:46,750
I'm on my way now

222
00:17:44,000 --> 00:17:46,750
Stay right where you are!

223
00:17:44,000 --> 00:17:46,750
This time I'm
gonna find you!

224
00:17:48,630 --> 00:17:49,670
<i>How...?</i>

225
00:18:04,680 --> 00:18:05,270
Oh!

226
00:18:16,400 --> 00:18:18,160
Hananoi-kun!

227
00:18:33,960 --> 00:18:35,170
<i>How?</i>

228
00:18:40,390 --> 00:18:42,050
Ow... ow, ow.

229
00:18:42,050 --> 00:18:43,810
S-Sorry!

230
00:18:44,470 --> 00:18:48,430
But I found you!

231
00:18:52,150 --> 00:18:55,940
A-Are you okay?! Are you hurt? 
Did you hit anything?

232
00:18:56,610 --> 00:19:01,940
No, I'm okay! You caught me, Hananoi-kun.

233
00:19:04,240 --> 00:19:06,700
But, Hotaru-chan, the memorial service...

234
00:19:07,160 --> 00:19:09,250
I snuck out partway through.

235
00:19:09,250 --> 00:19:09,960
Huh?

236
00:19:10,420 --> 00:19:14,380
Um, I realized it had to be today.

237
00:19:19,970 --> 00:19:23,090
Happy birthday, Hananoi-kun!

238
00:19:27,640 --> 00:19:31,600
You always make me so happy. Thank you!

239
00:19:34,270 --> 00:19:37,110
<i>How is it that you're always...</i>

240
00:19:39,030 --> 00:19:40,360
<i>like this?</i>

241
00:19:45,080 --> 00:19:48,700
<i>I love you so much!
 I want to be your number one.</i>

242
00:19:50,120 --> 00:19:54,040
<i>But... you don't have to put me first.</i>

243
00:19:54,920 --> 00:19:58,630
<i>As long as you stay with me forever...</i>

244
00:20:00,130 --> 00:20:03,090
Thank you, Hotaru-chan.

245
00:20:07,260 --> 00:20:08,600
<i>That's all I need.</i>

246
00:20:17,780 --> 00:20:19,940
The cherry blossoms sure are pretty.

247
00:20:19,940 --> 00:20:20,780
Yeah.

248
00:20:21,490 --> 00:20:25,530
There's hardly any point 
in seeing them alone.

249
00:20:27,030 --> 00:20:30,700
Hey, Hananoi-kun, I can tell 
you're trying to act normal,

250
00:20:30,700 --> 00:20:32,710
but was today really hard for you?

251
00:20:32,710 --> 00:20:33,500
Uh...

252
00:20:34,380 --> 00:20:40,290
I mean, it'd be a little difficult for me
 to stay with you all of the time,

253
00:20:40,590 --> 00:20:45,540
but whenever you aren't doing okay, 
I definitely want to be with you.

254
00:20:46,210 --> 00:20:49,640
If you ever feel like that,
 just call me, okay?

255
00:20:50,720 --> 00:20:51,930
Promise me.

256
00:21:01,690 --> 00:21:08,230
<i>Will I really be able to 
keep a smile on her face going forward?</i>

257
00:21:15,520 --> 00:21:16,970
Wow!

258
00:21:17,920 --> 00:21:20,340
It's a cherry blossom blizzard!

259
00:21:21,940 --> 00:21:27,290
<i>Can a guy like me be with Hotaru-chan?
 Is that even allowed?</i>

260
00:21:30,910 --> 00:21:33,810
<i>No, I can do this.</i>

261
00:21:35,540 --> 00:21:38,860
<i>I'm not the boy who couldn't 
do anything for her anymore.</i>

262
00:21:50,370 --> 00:21:51,370
<i>From now on,</i>

263
00:21:52,300 --> 00:21:54,660
<i>I won't run away, no matter what.</i>

264
00:21:56,080 --> 00:21:59,330
<i>I'll stay and protect this 
girl from whatever happens.</i>

265
00:22:03,910 --> 00:22:07,310
<i>I want to be your soulmate.</i>

